I support early allocation. Trust Anchor IDs are long overdue.

Cheers,
Egor

On Friday, October 16th, 2026 at 16:55, Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com> wrote=
:

> Hi! After a request from and discussions with the authors of draft-ietf-=
tls-trust-anchor-ids [1], the chairs would like to determine whether there=
 is consensus to request an early code point assignment; see [2] about the=
 early allocation process. The code point in question is for 'trust_anchor=
s' in the TLS ExtensionType Values registry, see Section 12.1 of the I-D. =
As noted in [3], implementers have been using a value chosen at random and=
 it has been stable since the initial draft. Please let the list know by 3=
0 October 2023 if you support this early allocation.
> =


> NOTE: A new registry is defined in Section 12.3 of the I-D, but we canno=
t ask for early creation of a registry.
> =


> Cheers,
> spt (for the chairs)
> =


> [1] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/
> [2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc7120/
> [3] https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/tls/vD37D986i5YtFFvfLfkcte_WSx=
k/
